Falsifies `machine_discovery::riscv64::verification::a_counter_width_is_widened_before_the_specifications_off_by_one_is_undone`.

The defect: `from_raw` masks the width field with `0xff` instead of `0x3f`.

SBI v3.0 defines `counter_info[17:12]` as the width, six bits, one less than the
number of bits in the CSR. Six bits is `0x3f`, and a byte is `0xff`; the two
spellings look equally plausible beside a `u8` field, and the wider one quietly
takes two bits of the reserved range with it. The mask and the `+ 1` that undoes
the specification's off-by-one live in two different functions forty lines apart,
which is why this is worth a prover rather than a reader: nothing at either site
says what the other one assumes.

The value arrives from firmware in `sbiret.value`, so the reserved bits are not
guaranteed zero on a machine whose SBI implementation is not QEMU's.

Expected to fail: `assert!((1..=64).contains(&bits))`.

diff --git a/crates/machine_discovery/src/riscv64.rs b/crates/machine_discovery/src/riscv64.rs
index 0e391a88..c7431c9f 100644
--- a/crates/machine_discovery/src/riscv64.rs
+++ b/crates/machine_discovery/src/riscv64.rs
@@ -948,7 +948,7 @@ impl CounterInfo {
         CounterInfo {
             firmware: value >> 63 != 0,
             raw_csr: (value & 0xfff) as u16,
-            raw_width: ((value >> 12) & 0x3f) as u8,
+            raw_width: ((value >> 12) & 0xff) as u8,
         }
     }
 
